{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"candidate_id\": \"69119fab9d25319b3bf376eca634b13104ba76b7417416b85a2a64a4e78a6ab4\",\n  \"coverage\": [\n    \"Read full native PCB, relevant schematic sources, project rules, and supplied DRC/ERC/netlist/geometry records.\",\n    \"Reproduced configured DRC: 142 violations, 114 parity issues, zero unconnected items; all 13 error-level results are excluded.\",\n    \"Independently compared 659 schematic pin-to-net assignments against PCB pads: no missing pins or net-name mismatches.\",\n    \"Measured connector hole annuli and exported separate plated/unplated drill files.\",\n    \"Inspected saved ground copper and routed connections at all three starved thermals.\",\n    \"Checked CAN2 termination population, connectivity, and ideal resistance calculations; sampled power, heater, and ground routing geometry.\"\n  ],\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"assessment\": \"defect\",\n      \"condition\": \"Five unnumbered J1 holes are declared plated through holes with copper diameter equal to drill diameter: three at 4.0 mm and two at 2.2 mm.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"Lines 21686–21725; five unnumbered thru_hole pads\",\n          \"path\": \"inputs/project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"board.design_settings.rules.min_via_annular_width = 0.1; drc_exclusions contains these holes\",\n          \"path\": \"inputs/project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pro\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"violations[132:142]: padstack and annular_width, excluded=true\",\n          \"path\": \"work/drc/drc.json\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"j1_mechanical_holes; radial_annulus_mm = 0 for all five\",\n          \"path\": \"review-work/physical/experiments/physical-measurements.json\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"Lines 1564–1573; T10 and T12 emit all five holes as plated\",\n          \"path\": \"review-work/physical/experiments/drills/Polygonus-Universal-Base-PTH.drl\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"id\": \"physical-001\",\n      \"location\": \"J1 unnumbered holes at (71.95,35.49), (75.55,39.34), (120,28.49), (199.65,39.34), and (203.25,35.49) mm\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"Annulus = (pad diameter − drill diameter)/2 = 0 mm, below the configured 0.1 mm minimum. Drill export preserves their plated classification.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"This is a reproducible native padstack/rule violation, despite its exclusion. Whether these were intended as unplated locating holes remains unresolved; the evidence does not establish connector fit failure or fabrication rejection.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"title\": \"Five plated J1 holes have zero annular copper\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"assessment\": \"defect\",\n      \"condition\": \"Saved F.Cu ground reliefs at C15.2, U7.4, and C14.2 each resolve one spoke against a configured minimum of two.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"GND zone UUID bc540b8b-3ffa-4b00-b211-3a91191a1f6d, line 69477 onward; saved filled polygons\",\n          \"path\": \"inputs/project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"Lines 263–273: exclusions; board.design_settings.rules.min_resolved_spokes = 2\",\n          \"path\": \"inputs/project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pro\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"violations[94:97]: starved_thermal, actual 1, minimum 2, excluded=true\",\n          \"path\": \"work/drc/drc.json\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"thermal_pads: pad coordinates, connected 0.25 mm traces, and nearby ground vias\",\n          \"path\": \"review-work/physical/experiments/physical-measurements.json\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"Three saved F.Cu detail panels\",\n          \"path\": \"review-work/physical/experiments/saved-thermal-copper.png\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"id\": \"physical-002\",\n      \"location\": \"C15.2 (107.851547,98.755769), U7.4 (101.008268,102.683572), C14.2 (101.591948,104.291543) mm\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"The saved zone connections do not satisfy the native minimum spoke count; exclusions suppress disposition without changing copper.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Independent DRC reproduces all three violations. Each pad also has a routed ground connection toward a nearby via, so these findings establish a geometric rule violation, not an open ground or demonstrated thermal failure.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"title\": \"Three saved ground reliefs violate the spoke minimum\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"assessment\": \"concern\",\n      \"condition\": \"Both carrier CAN2 termination options, R36 and R37, are 120 ohms but DNP and excluded from assembly outputs.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"Lines 2665–2675; resistor UUID d69380f9-5487-4782-9ce9-0690df62e543; R36/R37 instances\",\n          \"path\": \"inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"R36 at lines 14742–14810; R37 at lines 18665–18733; DNP attributes\",\n          \"path\": \"inputs/project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"nets /CAN2+ and /CAN2-; components R36 and R37\",\n          \"path\": \"work/netlist/connectivity.json\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"CAN2_carrier_termination_cases and stated exclusions\",\n          \"path\": \"review-work/physical/experiments/termination-calculation.json\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"id\": \"physical-003\",\n      \"location\": \"Internal dual-wideband CAN2 network, R36/R37 and J2.73/J2.74\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"The saved carrier population contributes no resistive termination. Host-module or harness termination therefore determines the assembled bus loading.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"The native population is clear, but host/harness termination and electrical behavior are unverified. Ideal carrier-only alternatives are 120 ohms with one resistor and 60 ohms with both. Continuity checks cannot establish appropriate loading or waveform quality, so a communication failure is not asserted.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"title\": \"Internal CAN2 termination remains unestablished\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"Saved copper only; no refill or candidate modification. Commands, versions, configuration differences, assumptions, and outcomes are recorded in review-work/physical/experiments/review-notes.md.\",\n    \"No hardware resistance, CAN traffic, waveform, cable, rise-time, bus-rate, or host-module population testing.\",\n    \"No component pinout audit, 3D fit, module standoff clearance, fabrication-tolerance qualification, or manufacturing approval.\",\n    \"No ampacity, simultaneous-load, fuse-coordination, thermal, automotive-transient, ignition-energy, wideband-stability, or EMC qualification; widths and via counts do not establish these.\",\n    \"Ignored courtyard checks and the configured zero copper-edge minimum limit mechanical and clearance coverage. Integrated FOME-MC and the separate original as-received checkout were not reviewed.\"\n  ],\n  \"packet_sha256\": \"7443dc72bd7dc0c25527bd0f1550b7d74a74454d412e30e18634608d420b4731\",\n  \"role\": \"physical\",\n  \"run_id\": \"bafd7961-39b9-4a34-9b39-b7f108e82f07\",\n  \"schema\": \"agent-ee.review/1\"\n}"}}
